From 80d116185b152670b23c8a68dad1b430c4e40cc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: q56-scratch <q56@scratch>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:48:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] src: one declaration per static - element names, A8 slot
 joins, the memory-card name; camera_CalcAngles to INCLUDE_ASM (owner rulings
 Q65/Q79/Q84, step 14)

Every object step 15 makes a static gets ONE declaration, typed by evidence, before the switch; all byte-identical
(full build SHA1 == oracle, every object compared). Changed completed bodies, each needing layer-2, with keys:
memory/grind/q65-adoption/q56/adopt/body_hashes.txt (step14).
- D_800A3468 (text1b_tu1c): the file's `s32`; func_80060A68 reads it through `#define OB ((struct Ob
  *)D_800A3468)` instead of a block-scope `extern struct Ob *`. The comment above func_80060A68 that cited a
  sibling's `extern s32 *D_800A3468;` now says that declaration existed then and is a single `s32` now.
- Per-word element names (layer-2 round 1, step-15 finding 1): g_anim_hit_flags s16[2] / g_anim_hit_data
  s32[2] (func_800420E8 indexes both with a0 < 2; g_anim_counter and D_800A3388 were their element 1),
  D_800A344C u32[2] / D_800A3454 s32[2] (per-lane pairs; D_800A3450 / D_800A3458 were element 1),
  D_800A35C8 s16[2] (declaration completed).
- (A8, owner ruling Q79, rules: 8c57bc4ab; probe memory/grind/q65-adoption/q56/adopt/lcomm_align_probe.*):
  Sony places every `.lcomm` static 4-aligned, so each gp-reached s16 name at a 2-mod-4 address is the
  second halfword of its slot's static: D_800A33C8[2] (was D_800A33C8 + D_800A33CA), D_800A33E8[2]
  (+ D_800A33EA; text1b already indexed `(&D_800A33E8)[idx]`), D_800A345C[2] (+ D_800A345E),
  D_800A350C[2] (+ D_800A350E; `&D_800A350C` is the pair pointer passed to func_800692C0), D_800A3510[2]
  (+ D_800A3512).
- Owner ruling Q84 (rules: 215f2d11a): camera_CalcAngles, the only writer of the D_800A33C8 pair, returns to
  INCLUDE_ASM (asm/funcs/camera_CalcAngles.s, func_80047384.s with its label renamed; as s16[2] our cc1 -G0
  spends one more instruction in every spelling measured, memory/grind/camera_CalcAngles/) and is re-queued
  active (engine queue reopen); the D_800A33CA row stays for its asm.
- The memory-card file name is its own object (layer-2 round 2, step-15 finding 5): code6cac_c_mid's
  `const u32 D_80010A2C[38]` becomes `D_80010A2C[32]` plus `const char D_80010AAC[] = "BASLUS-00663BUSHIDO2";`.
  Evidence: func_80038170 copies exactly 0x40 halfwords (128 bytes) of D_80010A2C; D_800A31F0's original word
  is 0x80010AAC (the string's address); the string is 21 bytes with its terminator and the 3 zero bytes after
  it are the file's rodata padding. The rodata comment above it is rewritten to say so. The symbol-file row
  `D_80010A2C = 0x80010A2C;` that pinned the C-defined object goes. Noted for the rodata cleanup, not changed:
  D_800109EC is declared [16] (64 bytes) but func_80038170 copies 0x10 halfwords (32 bytes); its last 32 bytes
  are zero.
- Symbol-file rows of the retired element names go where nothing names them any more.
